<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5127" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμέλει</span></b> , properly imper. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμελέω</span> (cf. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμέλησον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DMort.</u>
					5.2
				</span></i>
			), <i>never mind, do not trouble yourself,</i> esp. to begin
			an answer, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				877
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Decl.</u>
				20.18
			</span></i>:—hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as Adv., <i>doubtless, by all means, of
				course,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				368
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				488
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				82a
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.4.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Sam.</u>
				8
			</span></i>; freq. ironically, as <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				532
			</span></i>; freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
			</span></i> to introduce a subject, <i><span class="en">
				13.1
			</span></i>, al., or a further point, <i><span class="en">
				2.9
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>for instance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				6.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DDeor.</u>
				25.1
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>at any rate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Nigr.</u>
				26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				10.2.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>and indeed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.16
			</span></i> W., <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				1.2.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				7.4.1
			</span></i>; <i>and so,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				2.22.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.6.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>actually,</i> to give emphasis, <i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				2.3
			</span></i>, al. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμέλεια</span></b> , ἡ, <i>indifference, negligence,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.122
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.38
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν</span>
			<i>towards</i> the gods, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				905b
			</span></i>, cf. ib.<i><span class="en">
				903a
			</span></i>: also in pl., <i>negligences,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				443a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1370a15
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
